// Generated once from public/fonts/Boldonse-Regular.ttf and
// public/icons/3d/stopwatch.webp (resized to 280x280 PNG) — inlined as
// build-time constants rather than self-fetched over HTTP at request time.
// A self-fetch (request.nextUrl.origin + '/fonts/...') was tried first and
// failed in a way only visible when actually tested against a real Vercel
// deployment: preview URLs sit behind Vercel's SSO deployment protection
// (confirmed via get_project_deployment_protection: enabled for
// 'all_except_custom_domains'), and the *incoming* request being
// authenticated doesn't carry over to this route's own outbound self-fetch
// — that fetch got an HTML SSO interstitial back instead of the font file,
// which Satori then failed to parse ("Unsupported OpenType signature
// <!DO"). Production sits on an exempted custom domain, so that specific
// failure likely wouldn't reproduce there — but a request-time dependency
// on this deployment's own reachability/auth state is exactly the kind of
// environment-specific fragility this route has already hit three
// different ways (see the file-level comment in route.ts). Inlining
// removes the dependency entirely, for every environment.
export const BOLDONSE_TTF_BASE64 = "";
export const STOPWATCH_ICON_PNG_BASE64 = "";
